meta {
  name: Test Desktop Burst
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/test-desktop-batch?count=3
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  count: 3
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Notifications — Test Desktop Burst (coalescing)

  Fires a TEST burst of `count` simulated alerts to verify that MANY alerts in one
  scan tick coalesce into a SINGLE desktop banner instead of spamming one per alert.

  - `count=1`  → one normal banner: `ORB UP AAPL 🟢 Buy`
  - `count>=2` → one summary banner titled `Trading Alerts (N)` with body like
    `AAPL 🟢Buy, NVDA 🔴Sell, PLTR 🟢Buy`

  This mirrors how the live engine behaves: alerts fired in the same minute are
  buffered and flushed as one coalesced banner (individual alerts still go to
  Telegram and the logs separately).

  ## Query
  - `count` — number of simulated alerts (default 3, capped at 20).

  ## Response (200)
  { desktopEnabled, sent, count, note, timestamp }
  - `desktopEnabled=false` → feature off or not on macOS.
}
